@startuml
title Environment lifecycle (owned by preview-hub)

[*] --> REQUESTED : up (CreateEnvironment)
REQUESTED --> RESOLVING : lock held
RESOLVING --> BUILDING : all refs resolved to commits
BUILDING --> STARTING : images exist for every (service, sha)
STARTING --> READY : every service HEALTHY within timeout
READY --> UPDATING : update --set svc=ref (UpdateEnvironment)
UPDATING --> BUILDING : changed services re-resolved
READY --> READY : up with identical refs (idempotent no-op)
REQUESTED --> FAILED : resolve error
RESOLVING --> FAILED : ref not found / manifest invalid
BUILDING --> FAILED : build error
STARTING --> FAILED : start / migrate / health timeout
UPDATING --> FAILED : any update error
FAILED --> UPDATING : update (retry with new refs)
READY --> DELETING : down / TTL expired
FAILED --> DELETING : down / TTL expired
DELETING --> DELETED : label inventory empty
DELETING --> DELETING : leftovers -> retry down
DELETED --> [*]

note right of FAILED
  Objects stay for inspection.
  Stale RUNNING op (pid gone, heartbeat > 10 min)
  moves any in-flight state to FAILED.
end note
note right of DELETED
  Terminal. Name becomes reusable.
  down on DELETED / unknown name = no-op sweep by label.
end note
note left of READY
  Forbidden: up with different refs on an active name
  (must be explicit update); any transition without the env lock.
end note
@enduml
